.TH start-cli-server-trusted-keys 1  "trusted-keys "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys \- Manage the keys this server trusts for packages and StartOS updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli server trusted\-keys\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the keys this server trusts for packages and StartOS updates
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-add(1)
Import public keys; newly added keys are trusted for packages
.TP
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-list(1)
List trusted keys and what each is trusted for
.TP
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-remove(1)
Remove a trusted key
.TP
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-update(1)
Rename a trusted key and set what it is trusted for
